---

Specimens in a project that uses the `Invertebrate zoology` catalog format show
the invertebrate form. Sex and life stage work the same way in every taxon
group; see [Measurements](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/).

{% aside type="caution" %}

Invertebrate zoology support is in beta. Check exports against your collection's
requirements before relying on them.

{% /aside %}

## Measurements

The ecological-interaction section is visible by default. Use
`Show specimen morphometrics` to reveal or hide the measurement fields; saved
morphometric values automatically reopen that section.

- `Sex`: select from the configured specimen-sex vocabulary.
- `Life stage`: select from the configured life-stage vocabulary.
- `Caste`: the caste of a social insect, when applicable.
- Ecological interactions: `Host organism` and `Host part`.
- Optional morphometrics: `Head width (mm)`, `Body length (mm)`,
  `Upper wingspan (mm)`, and `Lower wingspan (mm)`.
- `Remarks`: additional ecological or specimen notes.

## Environmental conditions

Environmental conditions are not specimen attributes. Record canopy cover on
the site under `Site Attributes`, and temperature, humidity, pH, dissolved
oxygen, and flow velocity on the collecting event's
[environmental data](/en/usages/events/).

## Parts and parasites

Invertebrate catalogs do not show parasite-detection fields or the parasite tab.
